=== HINT 1: WSAStartup ===
WSADATA wsa;
WSAStartup(MAKEWORD(2,2), &wsa);

=== HINT 2: Non-blocking connect ===
u_long mode = 1;
ioctlsocket(s, FIONBIO, &mode);
connect(s, (struct sockaddr*)&addr, sizeof(addr));
// Returns WSAEWOULDBLOCK - expected for non-blocking

=== HINT 3: select() to check result ===
fd_set wset, eset;
FD_ZERO(&wset); FD_ZERO(&eset);
FD_SET(s, &wset); FD_SET(s, &eset);
struct timeval tv = { 0, 200000 };
int sel = select(0, NULL, &wset, &eset, &tv);
// sel > 0 and FD_ISSET(s, &wset) -> OPEN
// sel > 0 and FD_ISSET(s, &eset) -> CLOSED (CONNREFUSED)
// sel == 0 -> FILTERED (timeout)

=== KEY INSIGHT ===
connect-scan leaves a full 3-way handshake - noisy, logged by firewalls/IDS.
SYN scan (raw socket, send SYN, parse SYN-ACK/RST) is stealthier but requires
root/admin and raw socket access.
Half-open scan: RST immediately after SYN-ACK - no established connection logged.
UDP scan: send empty datagram; ICMP port-unreachable = closed, no response = open/filtered.
Rate limiting: scan too fast -> IDS/firewall detection. Add delay between ports.
